Things should do after installing the zip file of the project above
there are 3 ways mentioned below
1. just preview of ui immediately.
2. installing zip and unfolding that in your local system.
3. running the overall project in DOCKER FILE.
====================================================================================================================================

WAY-1.         LIVE PREVIEW.
    CLICK the URL : disaster-relief-coordination-hub/src/main/resources/static/index.html
        you can run this file for UI preview .
====================================================================================================================================

WAY-2. -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. unzip the disaster-relief-coordination-hub.zip
                       │
                       ▼
2. double-click the "run.bat"
                       │
                       ▼
3. Maven Wrapper (mvnw) automatically triggers:
   ├── Reads pom.xml
   ├── Automatically downloads Spring Boot 3.2.5, Embedded Tomcat, and H2 database
   └── Compiles all 4 layers of your Java code
                       │
                       ▼
4. Embedded Tomcat boots up on port 8080
                       │
                       ▼
5. H2 in-memory database automatically creates tables & seeds data from data.sql
                       │
                       ▼
6. Ready! User opens http://localhost:8080 in their browser

===========================================================================================================================

